 ## Schema compilation and caching

-- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled once at `register` time, so a schema that is not valid JSON Schema throws synchronously from `register` with an error message naming the offending tool ([validated by: throws at register time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L94), [validated by: throws at registration time for an uncompilable schema naming the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L10)).
-- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled at `register` time and reused on every `execute` call without re-reading or re-compiling `definition.inputSchema` ([validated by: compiles a static tool schema once at register time and reuses it across multiple execute calls](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L116)).
-- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition on each `execute` call and validates against the `inputSchema` returned for that call, caching compiled validators by schema object reference (`WeakMap`) so distinct returned schemas each enforce their own rules ([validated by: re-evaluates dynamic function-valued tool definitions and validates against the schema current at that call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L142)).
